  "body": "Step 10.{1,2} for an async send() ( https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-xmlhttprequest-send ) fire 'loadstart'(s). The event handling code could side-effect the state of the XHR object (calling abort() or re-initiate another send() by re-opening), should it so wish.\r\n\r\nThe spec doesn't _appear_ to account for that possibility upon return and continuing on to step 10.3.\r\n\r\nThis came up (indirectly) via https://crbug.com/642242",
